            "Waller's book put 400 into the Wikipedia article on the day it was created, 8 August 2008. A "
            "new reading of printed editions.",
            "The anonymous Basel chronicle (written before 1537) restored to 1518: its manuscript reads "
            "1518; its editor, the Basel historian August Bernoulli, moved it to 1418 in 1902 because of "
            "Schilter's misdated council orders. It is the earliest narrative outside Strasbourg; its "
            "wording matches, in prose, six verses from an unidentified Strasbourg manuscript chronicle "
            "that Schilter printed in 1698 under the same wrong year; and it is the earliest source for "
            "\"hundreds\" as a round plural (the Imlin chronicle, written at the time, gives the figure of "
            "more than 200): its \"several hundred\" is the formula that the verses give as \"many "
            "hundreds\", a stock expression rather than a tally. A new reading of a printed edition.",
            "The ergot hypothesis tested against reconstructed weather, for the first time in the "
            "literature that could be reached: a drought index of −6.8 for 1517 at Strasbourg in the Old "
            "World Drought Atlas (third driest summer of 1500–1600), a dry spring and a warm May and "
            "June; the cold June of 1518 is the one favourable sign, and it belongs to a crop not yet "
            "cut. The climate and price datasets are the one body of evidence not brought to the question "
            "before; the datasets are the published work of others, and their application here is new. "
            "The extraction from the atlas was run a second time from scratch and gives the same value "
            "(−6.787 at the Strasbourg cell).",
            "The outbreak ended in August: \"Dienstag post Adolphi\" is 31 August 1518 (St Adelphus falls "
            "on 29 August), rather than 29 September as Martin read it; the letter of 25 July says the "
            "sickness was ending. A calendar correction.",
            "The council's policy was containment rather than encouragement: drums restricted on 22 July, "
            "wagons to the shrine on 23 July, on 25 July a cooling diet and string music only, a general "
            "ban on 2 August, families and brotherhoods made responsible on 11 August. The platform on "
            "the horse market with people hired to dance with the sick, to drums and pipes, is "
            "Specklin's, written about 1580. The pilgrimage was imposed by the council (the Instruction "
            "of 23 July for the transport to the shrine), which weakens the reading of the dancing as a "
            "chosen rite; dancers who chose the rite appear only in Johann Wencker, a Strasbourg "
            "magistrate whose chronicle of 1637 copies Specklin. A new reading of the documents Martin "
            "printed.",
            "Waller's supporting details corrected: the English sweat of 1517, an epidemic fever of the "
            "period, is a misdating of 1529; the \"smallpox hospital\" is the Blatterhaus, the house for "
            "syphilis; the leper house shows no surge (eight inmates and two deaths in 1518 to 1519); the "
